What this solution actually does: Replicas_CDA is a timer-driven integration service that copies operational and reference data among CMS, TOMI, T24 views, SPEI, SPID, and TEF. A tick loads business dates and accounts, executes startup-only cleanup and cash-pooling work, refreshes balances, rates, customers, participants, pending operations, time deposits, and several reconciliation tables, and monitors BBVA through HSM-decrypted credentials and a certificate-authenticated TSEC request. The host gates work on three database-health probes, records service execution state through shared MUFG_T24 infrastructure, and uses a SimpleInjector async scope per tick.
