5. Architecture-Fit Note
Replicas_CDA is a scheduled, stateful integration workflow rather than an independently scalable request service. Its main risk is not the Windows Service host itself; it is loss of stage outcomes and partial state across multiple databases and security integrations. The lowest-risk sequence is therefore to modernize in place: first make every stage result explicit, add idempotent replay/partial-failure state, protect and bound HSM/TSEC calls, version dependencies, and add failure-path tests; then move to a supported .NET Worker Service with structured telemetry and health checks. An explicit workflow/saga engine may later improve auditability and resumability if volumes, recovery objectives, and cross-system compensation justify it. Serverless scheduling or a full microservices rewrite is not justified by current evidence and should not be chosen without measured tick duration, transaction volume, hosting constraints, idempotency guarantees, and operational ownership.
